# One truth per commit, on every machine.
#
# PRD-004 CTXHASH incident (2026-08-11): the same commit honestly reported
# PASS 224/224 on an LF checkout and FAIL 221/3 on this repo's own Windows
# autocrlf=true checkout, because a byte-level gate read working-tree bytes
# and the two machines materialized different bytes from the same blob.
# Verdicts of byte-reading gates must be a function of the COMMIT, never of
# the checkout platform — so working-tree materialization is pinned here.
#
# LF is the repo truth (the index was already 100% LF when this landed).
# Every modern Windows toolchain in use here (Python, Node, PowerShell 5.1,
# VS Code, uv, pnpm) consumes LF correctly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe batch parsing has documented quirks with LF (multi-line labels /
# call targets); keep the native format for the one interpreter that cares.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Pre-existing pins (predate the repo-wide rule; kept for the
# linguist-generated markers — the eol=lf part is now redundant but harmless).
packages/contracts/generated/*.json text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
engines/hermes_kernel/mcp_wrapper/schemas/*.json text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
tests/fixtures/*.json text eol=lf

# Explicit binary pins (belt over text=auto's content sniffing).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
